1
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:13,600
Grandpa, thank you so much
for saving Grandma.

2
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,320
The person you should thank is over there.

3
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,600
‎PREVIOUSLY

4
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:19,040
He asked me to come help you.

5
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,320
Hathaya is staying here.

6
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,560
I brought Hathaya back to help
with the development.

7
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,480
Papang's not at home.

8
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:29,120
I'm afraid he may have run away
like he threatened to before.

9
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:32,600
You're his father.
Don't you feel anything at all?

10
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:36,880
Yes, ma'am.

11
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:40,080
Any luck finding Papang?

12
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:43,200
Not yet. I sent Papang's picture
to the development's chat group

13
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:45,440
so security and residents
can look for him.

14
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:47,080
Have you told Ramil yet?

15
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,080
I called him already.

16
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,400
Then you go join Ramil.

17
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,280
I'll ask around at the shops
near the entrance.

18
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,640
Okay.

19
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,200
Any luck?

20
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:04,080
Nothing. We looked everywhere,
but no luck.

21
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,320
Are you sure Papang isn't hiding
in the house like last time?

22
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,840
I searched everywhere.

23
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,040
Why would Papang run away?

24
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:18,040
I asked at the shops near the entrance.

25
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:20,839
They said they saw Papang
running toward the main road.

26
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:25,760
And they also said
there's a child-abduction gang.

27
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:28,160
A few days ago, they kidnapped a child,

28
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:30,640
and the police still haven't caught them.

29
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:33,000
A child-abduction gang?

30
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,440
Get in.

31
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,280
Should we go back?

32
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:48,280
Let's not waste the trip.
Drive around one more time.

33
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:51,960
Go. Drive.

34
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:58,200
Where did Sanguansri go?

35
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,480
I asked where your madam went.

36
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:09,240
Papang ran away from home, Dad.
She went to help look for him.

37
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,680
Does no one in this house
understand a simple order?

38
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:14,480
I told her not to get involved
with that family.

39
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:18,160
She can deal with me when she gets back.

40
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:20,480
Dad.

41
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:24,080
I'm going out to help look for Papang.

42
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:28,120
What is wrong with everyone in this house?

43
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:30,880
Are you going to disobey me too?

44
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:39,840
I'm sorry, Dad,

45
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:42,160
but I have to help look for Papang.

46
00:05:43,720 --> 00:05:46,000
You dare disobey me, Raiwin?

47
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,640
If Ramil finds out

48
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:50,200
that Papang ran away
because of the lies you told him,

49
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:51,640
he won't let this go.

50
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,960
And what exactly can he do to me?

51
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:01,200
-Serve the rice.
-Yes, sir.

52
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:03,920
Your madam isn't here,
so you forgot how to work?

53
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,440
Dad, you taught me

54
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,440
that a politician needs
a good public image.

55
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,440
A reliable community figure.

56
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:15,160
That's exactly the image
I'm building right now.

57
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,760
Raiwin, get back here.

58
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:21,120
Dammit!

59
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:25,240
Damn that kid.
All he does is cause trouble.

60
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:27,200
Would you like your rice now, sir?

61
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:28,960
No! Get out.

62
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:30,800
I don't want to look at you.

63
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:34,440
That damn kid. It'd be better if he died.

64
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,520
There'd be one less problem to deal with.

65
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,760
Mommy.

66
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:01,280
Which way is Mommy's house?

67
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:11,080
Mommy. I'm hungry.

68
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,800
Someone said they saw Papang.

69
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:32,200
Are they sure it wasn't another child?

70
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,440
I showed them his picture.
They're sure it was him.

71
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:38,160
They said he was wearing
these exact clothes.

72
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,480
This is my fault.

73
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:44,360
I made him think I was abandoning him.
If anything happens to Papang,

74
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,600
I'll never forgive myself.

75
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,480
I'm sure Papang is safe.
Let's go find him.

76
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,000
Come on.

77
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:58,040
Any news, Officer?
Have you found my grandson?

78
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,160
Please keep looking for him.

79
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:08,240
Auntie. Let's go look for Papang.

80
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:12,600
Yes.

81
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,360
Daddy.

82
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,360
Where are you?

83
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:23,400
I miss you, Daddy.

84
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,240
Please come help me, Daddy.

85
00:08:35,919 --> 00:08:38,360
Daddy came to get me.

86
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,080
Daddy.

87
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Hey, little guy. Where are you going?

88
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,040
Why are you walking around
out here by yourself?

89
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,240
I'm trying to find Mommy,

90
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,520
but I don't remember the way home.

91
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,440
I want to go back to Daddy.

92
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:06,560
And where does your dad live?

93
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,800
Over there. There's a fountain
at the roundabout.

94
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:15,200
Oh, the fountain roundabout.
I know where that is.

95
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:18,560
I'm going that way anyway.
Want me to give you a ride home?

96
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,760
Okay? It's dark and deserted.

97
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,840
Your dad must be really worried.

98
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:27,160
Come with me.
I'll take you all the way home.

99
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,560
Play with toys.

100
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:30,680
Come on. Get in.

101
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,800
Come on. Get in.

102
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,960
Hop in. There are other kids in here.

103
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:42,480
You can sit together and play.
It'll be fun. Come on.

104
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,800
I told you to get in.

105
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:46,880
Do we have to force you?

106
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,360
-Go get him. Quickly.
-Help!

107
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,400
Help. Help!

108
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:00,880
That's it.

109
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:04,360
You're just going to tire yourself out.
Go wait in the AC van.

110
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,320
-Grab him.
-Wait.

111
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:10,360
Sit down. Just sit there and look cool.
I'll handle this kid myself.

112
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:13,360
I'm still mad about that kick he gave me.

113
00:10:16,400 --> 00:10:17,320
Hey!

114
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:19,720
-Let me go. Help.
-Come here. Quiet.

115
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:20,800
-Somebody help me.
-Come on.

116
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,480
-Quiet. Shut up.
-Somebody help me.

117
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,200
-Daddy's here. Daddy.
-Let go of my son.

118
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:29,160
Take care of the kid.

119
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:31,440
Wait. I'll handle him myself.

120
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:42,320
That was luck.

121
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,840
This time I'm serious.

122
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:47,320
I'm serious.

123
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:59,440
Quit sitting there like an idiot.
Come help me.

124
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:02,440
-Hurry up.
-Papang.

125
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:13,200
-Papang.
-Get in. Don't fight.

126
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:20,160
Come here.

127
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,520
Hit him. He can take it.

128
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,840
See? Doesn't even hurt him.

129
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,880
Hey. You said it doesn't hurt.

130
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:42,600
Wake up. Get up.

131
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:48,560
Auntie, watch out.

132
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,080
Stay behind me.

133
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,520
You really wanna die, huh?

134
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,800
Hathaya, get back.

135
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:07,080
Stop right there.

136
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,320
You think you're tough?

137
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,680
Time to pay you back.

138
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:24,320
What was that?

139
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:34,520
That was only a warning shot.
This time, I'll shoot for real.

140
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,680
Don't try anything. Drop your weapons.
The police are on their way.

141
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,040
Police?

142
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:16,000
Ms. Sanguansri called.

143
00:13:16,080 --> 00:13:18,080
They found Papang.

144
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:20,880
Everyone is at the police station now,
and they'll be coming back soon.

145
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,360
Come with me.

146
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,880
We're home.

147
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,680
Let me get the door for you. Just a sec.

148
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:52,200
Come on.

149
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,000
Alright.

150
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,960
We're home.

151
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,040
Daddy, what happened to you?

152
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:08,040
As long as you're safe,
Daddy doesn't hurt anymore.

153
00:14:19,280 --> 00:14:20,840
And Grandma

154
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:23,280
was worried about you too.

155
00:14:32,640 --> 00:14:36,400
You're safe now, sweetheart. Don't ever
do something like this again, okay?

156
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,400
Papang.

157
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,600
I told you not to run away from home.

158
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,840
Why did you do it?

159
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:54,960
I thought Daddy was gone.

160
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:56,800
I thought nobody loved me.

161
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,920
Why would you think that?

162
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,240
-Because--
-Ramil.

163
00:15:03,360 --> 00:15:04,680
Can I talk to Papang for a minute?

164
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:09,560
You must be hungry. Daddy will go
make you something to eat.

165
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,160
Then I'll head home now.

166
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,240
Papang.

167
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:34,040
Papang, I know you ran away

168
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:36,760
because you were hurt by the mean things
Grandpa said to you.

169
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,560
Your father doesn't
want to take care of you.

170
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,560
Everyone hates you.

171
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:46,800
No one loves you. Everyone here hates you.

172
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,160
Grandpa didn't mean it.

173
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:53,640
He was arguing with Ramil

174
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:57,200
and was upset.
He took that anger out on you.

175
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:59,640
Then why did Grandpa say those things?

176
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:02,040
He didn't mean them.

177
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:05,280
When Grandpa heard that you ran away,

178
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:08,840
he got worried. That's why he told me

179
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:10,720
to come look for you.

180
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,320
Papang.

181
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:15,480
If you don't want Grandpa
and Daddy to fight again,

182
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,720
could you not tell Daddy
what Grandpa said?

183
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:24,920
Okay. I won't tell Daddy.

184
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,880
That's my good…

185
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,520
nephew.

186
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:37,400
Thank you for helping me, Uncle.

187
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:39,880
Go inside.

188
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,599
-Let's eat.
-Okay.

189
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:11,680
You still haven't answered me.

190
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:14,760
Why did you run away?

191
00:17:15,599 --> 00:17:18,400
I woke up and couldn't find you.

192
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:21,280
I thought you left me.

193
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,560
Papang.

194
00:17:25,640 --> 00:17:29,200
Remember this. Daddy loves you
more than anything.

195
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:33,200
Promise me

196
00:17:33,280 --> 00:17:34,880
that you'll never do this again.

197
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:37,600
I'm sorry. I promise.

198
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:39,800
Good. You promised.

199
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,200
Don't do this again,

200
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:43,560
-okay?
-Okay.

201
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,800
Let's eat then.

202
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,880
Eat plenty of vegetables.

203
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,960
Get some vegetables.

204
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,920
Eat some vegetables.
Let me see you eat some.

205
00:17:55,040 --> 00:17:57,120
Very good.

206
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:03,480
Where are my clothes?
Did you pack up my things?

207
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:12,800
You dared disobey me?

208
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,800
If you don't want
to live here, then leave.

209
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:18,000
Go live with your son.
Go live with your grandson.

210
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,040
Put this back in my room.

211
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:28,680
Go.

212
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:33,640
You've gotten pretty bold, Sanguansri.

213
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,880
If you aren't afraid of starving,
why live off me?

214
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:39,080
I wasn't trying to defy you.

215
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:42,440
Don't make excuses. Then why did you
go looking for that damn kid?

216
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,960
I went to help find my grandson

217
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:46,680
to keep Ramil from blaming you.

218
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,680
You lied to Papang and upset him

219
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:50,840
so badly that he ran away.

220
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:53,560
You think I'm afraid of Ramil?
He should be afraid of me.

221
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,840
I supported you
and those people for decades.

222
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:59,080
You've been living off me all this time.

223
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:03,000
I've been with you for more than 20 years.

224
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,800
Was all I did for nothing?

225
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:10,400
If that's all my love
and concern are worth to you,

226
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,160
then now I know my place.

227
00:19:14,280 --> 00:19:16,880
I'm nothing more than a servant

228
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:19,840
who works just for food and shelter.

229
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,360
And the reason I disobeyed you

230
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,080
was because I wanted to help Papang.

231
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:28,840
You may hate him and refuse to accept him,

232
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:31,840
but you still can't deny
that he's your own blood.

233
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:41,360
Go upstairs and get some rest.

234
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:45,040
You too. You're going over my head now?

235
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,480
I love you, and I'm worried
about you, Dad.

236
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:51,200
That's why I went to help look for Papang.

237
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:53,080
And I asked him

238
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:56,680
not to tell anyone that you
were the reason he ran away.

239
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:59,040
Are you insulting me?

240
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:01,040
That's not what I mean.

241
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:03,400
But if the kidnapping gang
had taken Papang

242
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:06,440
and something terrible had happened,
everyone would have blamed you.

243
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:10,680
Are you threatening me, Raiwin?

244
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:12,920
No one is threatening you.

245
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,960
Everyone is trying to protect you.

246
00:20:20,560 --> 00:20:22,440
Why are you interfering in my family?

247
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:25,760
You're an outsider. Get out.

248
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:29,520
If you weren't the reason Papang ran away,

249
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,240
I wouldn't have set foot in here.

250
00:20:32,280 --> 00:20:35,160
You're an adult with a respectable job.

251
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:37,400
You should feel bad for what you did,

252
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:41,040
yet you hurt a child
who just needs kindness

253
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:44,680
and love. If you can't show him kindness

254
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:46,440
or compassion,

255
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:49,880
then leave him alone. You have no right
to destroy his feelings like that.

256
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:51,560
Who do you think you are?

257
00:20:52,080 --> 00:20:54,720
What gives you the right to lecture me
in my own house? Get out.

258
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,320
I will.

259
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,480
But you need to hear me first.

260
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:02,920
This time, I'll turn a blind eye

261
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:04,800
to what you did.

262
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:08,720
But if you ever hurt Papang
like this again,

263
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:10,320
I won't let it go.

264
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:13,520
Get out, and don't ever
set foot in here again.

265
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:15,760
Do you understand?

266
00:21:15,840 --> 00:21:18,040
And don't ever let her
into this house again.

267
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,160
That goes for both of you.

268
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:23,760
Stay away from that woman.

269
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:27,520
Let's go.

270
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:34,560
You think you can challenge me?

271
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:36,760
You picked the wrong man.

272
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:49,440
Aunt Hathaya finished cooking.

273
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:50,800
Come on. Let's eat.

274
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:57,040
I will get you something to drink.
What do you want? Red soda?

275
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:12,240
Auntie knows the secret
between you and Uncle Raiwin.

276
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:19,160
You did a very good thing
by forgiving Grandpa.

277
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:31,440
You don't love me.
Why did you serve me food?

278
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:36,560
Who said I don't love you?
And I don't hate you either.

279
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,960
Feelings can change.

280
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:44,640
What about you?
Do you like me a little now?

281
00:22:53,440 --> 00:22:54,400
Stay behind me.

282
00:22:55,200 --> 00:22:57,240
Hathaya, get back.

283
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:09,240
-Well?
-Are you done talking yet?

284
00:23:17,560 --> 00:23:19,360
So we can finally eat.

285
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:25,480
Thank you for helping me.

286
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:30,880
Thank you, Mother…

287
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:35,080
Mother witch.

288
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:38,800
-Little imp.
-Witch.

289
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:40,120
-Little imp.
-Witch.

290
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,440
-Little imp.
-Witch.

291
00:23:41,520 --> 00:23:44,760
All right, little imp and witch.
The wizard has arrived.

292
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:48,840
Finish everything on your plate.
If you don't,

293
00:23:48,920 --> 00:23:50,520
I'll turn you into a little imp.

294
00:23:51,120 --> 00:23:51,960
Little imp.

295
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:54,880
-Witch.
-Little imp.

296
00:23:54,960 --> 00:23:57,720
-Witch.
-Eat first, little imp and witch.

297
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:00,640
Little imp. Witch.

298
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:05,640
-Want some too, witch?
-No, thanks.

299
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:11,200
Let's eat.

300
00:24:17,800 --> 00:24:19,320
How's your arm?

301
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:22,000
It's okay. It's getting better.

302
00:24:22,760 --> 00:24:26,560
Don't forget your medicine,
and try not to use that arm too much.

303
00:24:29,080 --> 00:24:32,240
Thank you for helping take care of Papang.

304
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:34,080
It's okay.

305
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:37,080
He may be stubborn
and may not like me very much,

306
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:40,680
but he's still a child, and I feel sorry
for what he's going through.

307
00:24:42,840 --> 00:24:44,800
I'll take the best care of him I can,

308
00:24:44,880 --> 00:24:47,280
and I'll keep trying to reach Nuchwara
so she can come get him.

309
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,400
I hope it works out.

310
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:51,880
Thanks.

311
00:24:57,520 --> 00:24:59,680
There are a lot of customers
looking at houses today.

312
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:02,280
Are you running some special promotion?

313
00:25:03,800 --> 00:25:05,040
Not that I know of.

314
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,400
I need to go take care of them.
See you later.

315
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,240
Aren't you going to welcome them?

316
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:22,600
Well…

317
00:25:23,840 --> 00:25:25,760
Hello. Hello.

318
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:27,120
Hello. Hello.

319
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:32,520
Hello, Uncle. Are you here
to look at a house?

320
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:35,160
I brought some customers.

321
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:36,920
They're all people I know.

322
00:25:38,120 --> 00:25:40,000
Thank you so much, Uncle.

323
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:44,520
Why are you thanking me?
I didn't bring those customers for you.

324
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:49,080
Please take good care of them.

325
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:57,080
Thank you so much
for bringing customers to me, Uncle.

326
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,360
You really didn't have to.

327
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:00,320
Don't worry about it, Chayanee.

328
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:04,600
You'll be joining my family soon enough.

329
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:07,360
Anything I promised you,

330
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,120
I'll do everything I can to deliver.

331
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:12,640
That way, Mr. Pichai,
your grandpa, can be proud

332
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:14,240
of his favorite granddaughter.

333
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:17,400
By the way, I brought

334
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:19,240
the customers all the way here.

335
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:22,280
Do you have any good promotions
for my friends?

336
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:26,240
Any customers you recommend
are premium customers.

337
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:28,800
I'll give them a special promotion
with free air conditioners

338
00:26:28,880 --> 00:26:32,320
and kitchen appliances. Plus,
if they fail to qualify for financing,

339
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:35,320
I'll refund their reservation deposit
in full.

340
00:26:38,080 --> 00:26:40,960
That's what I like to hear.

341
00:26:41,040 --> 00:26:43,320
A new-generation executive has to be bold.

342
00:26:43,400 --> 00:26:47,320
Chaya, you still need to check each
customer's income information carefully.

343
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:51,200
Hathaya, you don't need
to teach me how to do my job.

344
00:26:51,960 --> 00:26:54,520
I've been doing this for a long time,
and I've never made a mistake.

345
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:56,240
Why don't you spend your time finding

346
00:26:56,320 --> 00:26:58,760
half as many customers as I have?

347
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:06,560
Uncle, please come to the VIP lounge.

348
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:07,480
Right over there.

349
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:20,120
Are you interested?

350
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:22,320
I can recommend
some good promotions for you.

351
00:27:22,840 --> 00:27:26,480
The house is beautiful, and the promotions
are good. I like it. I'll reserve one.

352
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,200
Please come over to the desk.

353
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:30,280
Where is Miss Chayanee?

354
00:27:31,560 --> 00:27:32,480
Why?

355
00:27:37,320 --> 00:27:39,480
Thank you for taking care

356
00:27:39,560 --> 00:27:41,440
of my customers, Hathaya.

357
00:27:45,560 --> 00:27:47,440
Mr. Saksit referred you, right?

358
00:27:47,520 --> 00:27:50,440
Yes. Mr. Saksit specifically told me
to make my reservation with you.

359
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:53,080
He said you have a special VIP promotion.

360
00:27:53,680 --> 00:27:56,080
That's right. Please have a seat.

361
00:28:06,280 --> 00:28:07,800
That wasn't very nice.

362
00:28:07,880 --> 00:28:10,760
It was her customer, but she had
someone else do all the work.

363
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:14,400
It's okay. No matter whose customer it is,

364
00:28:14,480 --> 00:28:16,720
the development still benefits.

365
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:18,680
Miss Chayanee gets all the credit,

366
00:28:18,760 --> 00:28:21,600
and your reservation numbers
are already really low this month.

367
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:24,400
There are still several days left, Ploy.

368
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,440
I'll work harder.

369
00:28:33,160 --> 00:28:34,800
How are this month's reservations?

370
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,440
These numbers are very high.

371
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:51,480
I've been doing everything I can.
I bring customers to the development,

372
00:28:51,560 --> 00:28:55,000
show them the model homes,
and persuade them to reserve immediately.

373
00:28:55,080 --> 00:28:57,680
I won't let down my reputation
as your favorite granddaughter.

374
00:29:00,040 --> 00:29:00,920
And yours?

375
00:29:04,520 --> 00:29:06,080
Ten houses.

376
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:11,400
You used to have
much higher reservation numbers.

377
00:29:11,480 --> 00:29:12,960
Looks like you've lost your touch.

378
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:15,520
My numbers aren't high,

379
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:18,200
but every one of my customers
is ready to pay cash.

380
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:24,560
And yours?

381
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:27,200
My customers are applying for financing.

382
00:29:27,720 --> 00:29:31,520
I already sent their applications
to the banks for assessment.

383
00:29:31,600 --> 00:29:34,440
Besides, Uncle Saksit referred them,

384
00:29:34,520 --> 00:29:36,000
so there shouldn't be any issues.

385
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:38,880
Don't take unnecessary risks.

386
00:29:39,400 --> 00:29:42,400
If they don't qualify, they lose time,

387
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:44,480
and we lose opportunities.

388
00:29:46,080 --> 00:29:47,120
And also,

389
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:50,720
what promotion did you use
to get numbers this high?

390
00:29:51,840 --> 00:29:55,160
The usual, free air conditioners
and kitchen appliances.

391
00:29:56,240 --> 00:29:57,960
The reason the numbers are so high

392
00:29:58,040 --> 00:30:00,200
is because Uncle Saksit
helped bring in customers.

393
00:30:00,280 --> 00:30:02,440
He wanted to help you and me.

394
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:08,920
With the economy slowing down like this,

395
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:15,880
do not use a promotion that refunds
their deposit if financing falls through.

396
00:30:16,520 --> 00:30:18,040
The risk is far too high.

397
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:20,280
Yes, Grandpa.

398
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:23,000
I definitely won't use that promotion.

399
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:30,960
Chaya, you shouldn't lie to Grandpa.

400
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:35,680
Come on, Hathaya.

401
00:30:36,920 --> 00:30:39,920
Low sales don't mean
you have to be a tattletale.

402
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:42,000
I'm not tattling.

403
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:44,920
If I wanted to, I would've told
Grandpa the truth just now.

404
00:30:45,680 --> 00:30:47,080
I didn't lie.

405
00:30:47,640 --> 00:30:50,920
I simply didn't mention it
because I didn't want Grandpa to worry.

406
00:30:52,360 --> 00:30:54,960
I'm confident Mr. Saksit's customers

407
00:30:55,040 --> 00:30:57,960
are respectable people
who will definitely qualify for financing.

408
00:30:58,800 --> 00:31:01,000
And another thing, Hathaya.

409
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:04,280
I've told you before

410
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:06,400
not to lecture me.

411
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:09,520
You should worry about yourself.

412
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:11,680
Your reservation numbers are this low.

413
00:31:12,360 --> 00:31:14,680
If you can't handle sales, then give it up

414
00:31:14,760 --> 00:31:18,440
and go back to hauling
bricks and cement. Go back

415
00:31:19,040 --> 00:31:20,360
where you belong.

416
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,600
Chayanee.

417
00:31:25,600 --> 00:31:26,440
Uncle Saksit.

418
00:31:29,160 --> 00:31:33,400
I brought you even more customers
who want to buy houses.

419
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:35,600
They're waiting at the model home.

420
00:31:36,240 --> 00:31:37,760
Thank you, Uncle.

421
00:31:37,840 --> 00:31:39,840
You're so sweet to me.

422
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:43,040
I haven't forgotten
what you asked me to do.

423
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:46,640
Then I'll go take care of the customers.

424
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:58,320
When I love someone,
I treat them very well.

425
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:02,080
But when I hate someone,

426
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:04,960
I hate them until the day I die.

427
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:18,520
Hello, ma'am.

428
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:21,200
What?

429
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:24,840
Okay.

430
00:32:34,880 --> 00:32:38,320
She came in, immediately took charge,
and then told me to go home.

431
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:39,920
She said she'd handle Papang herself.

432
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:42,320
Thank you.

433
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:43,520
Where is she now?

434
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:45,640
Inside.

435
00:32:47,080 --> 00:32:47,920
Okay.

436
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:57,880
Papang,

437
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:59,640
how much do you love Mommy?

438
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:02,560
I love you more than anyone, Mommy.

439
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:06,080
Mommy loves you more than anyone too.

440
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:08,040
And I love Daddy
as much as the whole universe.

441
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:10,000
Hello.

442
00:33:10,640 --> 00:33:13,200
Auntie, you're back.

443
00:33:13,280 --> 00:33:14,640
Where's Daddy?

444
00:33:15,240 --> 00:33:17,400
Daddy has a little more work to do.
He'll be home soon.

445
00:33:17,480 --> 00:33:19,360
I was worried about you,
so I came back first.

446
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:21,360
Okay.

447
00:33:22,560 --> 00:33:26,040
Papang, go upstairs
and play your game for a while.

448
00:33:26,120 --> 00:33:27,400
Okay.

449
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:45,000
You're back.

450
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:48,440
Papang is so happy.
He's really glad you're here.

451
00:33:48,520 --> 00:33:50,640
Of course. I'm his mother.

452
00:33:51,760 --> 00:33:55,040
Naturally, he loves me
and wants to be with me,

453
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,920
not some outsider
who isn't his mother or father.

454
00:34:02,520 --> 00:34:04,720
And that "hello" you gave me earlier?

455
00:34:04,800 --> 00:34:06,160
Let's change it to "goodbye".

456
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:08,400
Where do you want me to go?

457
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:10,840
We're going to live here
together as a family.

458
00:34:10,920 --> 00:34:13,120
This house doesn't need you.

459
00:34:13,679 --> 00:34:15,960
I'm Ramil's wife.

460
00:34:16,040 --> 00:34:18,159
Not some fake wife like you.

461
00:34:20,560 --> 00:34:24,360
I know you and Ramil
aren't romantically involved.

462
00:34:26,239 --> 00:34:28,679
So hurry upstairs,
pack your things, and get out.

463
00:34:31,639 --> 00:34:32,880
Go.

464
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:36,800
I told you to leave,
and you're still here. Shameless.

465
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:40,199
I'm sorry,

466
00:34:41,120 --> 00:34:45,159
but you're not the one who gets
to decide whether I stay or leave.

467
00:34:45,239 --> 00:34:46,880
You don't own this house.

468
00:34:47,679 --> 00:34:48,920
You're staying here too.

469
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:51,199
I told you.

470
00:34:51,719 --> 00:34:53,960
I'm Ramil's wife.

471
00:34:54,960 --> 00:34:57,960
I said go upstairs
and pack your clothes. Go.

472
00:34:59,040 --> 00:35:00,200
Let go of her.

473
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Hathaya.

474
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:09,400
Go get some rest.

475
00:35:10,680 --> 00:35:12,320
I'm not finished talking to this woman.

476
00:35:12,920 --> 00:35:14,360
Her name is Hathaya.

477
00:35:14,960 --> 00:35:16,680
You should address her properly.

478
00:35:18,240 --> 00:35:19,400
I need to talk to you.

479
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:21,400
Come here.

480
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:29,480
Let go. You're hurting me.

481
00:35:31,160 --> 00:35:32,120
Where have you been?

482
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:35,760
You said you wouldn't be gone long,
then you left your son here.

483
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:38,600
Do you have any idea
how much he missed you?

484
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:39,960
He even ran away from home.

485
00:35:40,040 --> 00:35:41,840
I was working.

486
00:35:42,720 --> 00:35:45,440
If I don't work, how am I
supposed to support my child?

487
00:35:45,520 --> 00:35:47,400
I'm a single mother.

488
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:50,080
Nobody just hands me money for free.

489
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:52,560
And it's not my fault

490
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:56,520
he ran away. It's yours.

491
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,360
When he lives with me,

492
00:36:00,440 --> 00:36:02,520
he never behaves like this.

493
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:06,720
Maybe that woman upset my son so badly

494
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:08,280
that he ran away.

495
00:36:08,920 --> 00:36:09,840
Enough.

496
00:36:10,640 --> 00:36:12,520
I'm not wasting time arguing with you.

497
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:16,320
If you want to blame me,

498
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:18,640
fine, I'll take responsibility.

499
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:20,720
But it's good that you're back.

500
00:36:20,800 --> 00:36:23,800
I can pack Papang's things,
and you can finally take him home.

501
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:25,240
I'm not leaving.

502
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:26,960
My son and I are staying here.

503
00:36:27,040 --> 00:36:28,120
What did you say?

504
00:36:28,200 --> 00:36:31,880
You know he's been starved for affection.

505
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:34,160
He needs love from both of us.

506
00:36:34,240 --> 00:36:35,920
I'm going to live here,

507
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,880
so we can be together as a family.
Father, mother, and son.

508
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:42,840
But we're only friends.
I've never loved you.

509
00:36:42,920 --> 00:36:44,880
You may never have loved me,

510
00:36:45,680 --> 00:36:47,800
but you shouldn't forget
the promise you made.

511
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:52,960
Stop.

512
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,960
-Let go of me.
-What are you doing? Let go.

513
00:36:56,040 --> 00:36:57,400
I said, let me go.

514
00:36:57,480 --> 00:37:00,200
-You're pregnant. Stop.
-I want to die.

515
00:37:00,280 --> 00:37:03,840
Your brother doesn't
love me anymore. Let me go.

516
00:37:06,200 --> 00:37:09,400
What are you doing? You're having a baby.

517
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:13,160
When the baby is born

518
00:37:13,240 --> 00:37:16,240
and asks who the father is,
what am I supposed to say?

519
00:37:17,680 --> 00:37:19,720
Tell the child I'm the father.

520
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:26,880
Nuch.

521
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:30,080
Please don't hurt yourself.

522
00:37:32,240 --> 00:37:34,080
And stay away from Raiwin from now on.

523
00:37:38,080 --> 00:37:39,440
I'll claim the baby as mine.

524
00:37:47,960 --> 00:37:49,480
You promised me

525
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:51,400
you wouldn't let him suffer.

526
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:53,800
Fine. I'll tell him

527
00:37:53,880 --> 00:37:56,840
you're not really his dad and that
the two of us don't love each other.

528
00:37:56,920 --> 00:37:59,600
Then we'll see what happens

529
00:37:59,680 --> 00:38:00,680
when he learns the truth.

530
00:38:08,240 --> 00:38:10,800
Daddy. Daddy's home.

531
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:11,920
Papang.

532
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:21,440
What were you and Mommy talking about?

533
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:25,920
Mommy and Daddy were talking
about something important.

534
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:30,720
Papang, listen to me.

535
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:33,560
-Mommy and Daddy--
-Love each other very much.

536
00:38:34,640 --> 00:38:37,960
Mommy and Daddy

537
00:38:38,960 --> 00:38:41,040
-love each other very much.
-That's right.

538
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:44,240
Mommy and Daddy love each other very much,

539
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:47,840
and we're going
to move in here with Daddy.

540
00:38:47,920 --> 00:38:49,000
I'm not going anywhere.

541
00:38:49,960 --> 00:38:52,840
Yay. I'm the happiest boy in the world.

542
00:38:55,960 --> 00:38:59,120
I'm so happy.

543
00:38:59,200 --> 00:39:00,360
Good.

544
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:35,600
Warm soy milk.

545
00:39:37,600 --> 00:39:38,840
Thank you.

546
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:41,560
Are you tired?

547
00:39:48,200 --> 00:39:49,280
Yeah, I am.

548
00:39:50,760 --> 00:39:51,720
But what can I do?

549
00:39:53,000 --> 00:39:54,720
Life goes on.

550
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:57,960
Sometimes we don't get to choose.

551
00:39:59,680 --> 00:40:00,720
No.

552
00:40:01,880 --> 00:40:03,200
I did choose.

553
00:40:05,360 --> 00:40:07,240
I chose to protect Papang.

554
00:40:09,040 --> 00:40:10,080
So I must face it.

555
00:40:12,400 --> 00:40:14,440
I admire what you're doing.

556
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:22,800
And I won't let you fight this alone.

557
00:40:25,160 --> 00:40:26,600
I'll help you.

558
00:40:30,080 --> 00:40:30,960
And…

559
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:34,240
why would you help me?

560
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:36,880
You helped my family.

561
00:40:37,720 --> 00:40:39,520
I want to repay you.

562
00:40:49,160 --> 00:40:50,080
Thank you.

563
00:41:24,520 --> 00:41:27,440
Your reservation numbers are soaring.

564
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:29,480
My daughter is amazing.

565
00:41:30,080 --> 00:41:32,160
Uncle Saksit didn't disappoint us.

566
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:35,280
He promised to help us
as much as he could.

567
00:41:35,360 --> 00:41:38,080
But what about your workers?
Can they finish the houses on time?

568
00:41:39,160 --> 00:41:42,240
Don't worry about construction.
Pong is good.

569
00:41:42,320 --> 00:41:45,480
He's handled hundreds of major projects.

570
00:41:45,560 --> 00:41:46,600
He's a professional.

571
00:41:46,680 --> 00:41:47,840
Good.

572
00:41:48,360 --> 00:41:51,920
I want Grandpa to trust us
more than Hathaya.

573
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:54,440
You bring in plenty of customers,

574
00:41:54,520 --> 00:41:58,160
and I'll make sure Pong
gets the houses built quickly.

575
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:01,440
Before long, Hathaya and Ramil

576
00:42:01,520 --> 00:42:03,040
will both be pushed aside.

577
00:42:03,640 --> 00:42:06,400
On the next project, I'll convince Father

578
00:42:06,480 --> 00:42:08,000
to get rid of them.

579
00:42:08,080 --> 00:42:11,320
Come on. Let's go flatter him.

580
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:12,240
Yes.

581
00:42:15,120 --> 00:42:16,240
Madam, where are you going?

582
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:18,360
I'm going to see Father. Move.

583
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:20,080
You can't.

584
00:42:20,760 --> 00:42:21,600
What is it?

585
00:42:22,320 --> 00:42:23,520
So…

586
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:26,560
Pong's workers are gone.

587
00:42:26,640 --> 00:42:29,080
Gone? Where did they go?

588
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:30,200
I don't know.

589
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:33,400
All of them are gone.

590
00:42:36,760 --> 00:42:38,000
Chamoi,

591
00:42:38,720 --> 00:42:40,360
you're such a liar.

592
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:42,320
There are workers everywhere.

593
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:45,320
What were you talking about? Look.

594
00:42:45,400 --> 00:42:47,120
Madam,

595
00:42:47,200 --> 00:42:50,800
those are Ramil's workers.

596
00:42:50,880 --> 00:42:53,440
Pong's workers? Over there.

597
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:58,360
There isn't a single worker.

598
00:42:58,440 --> 00:43:01,680
The houses will never get built.
Mom, you have to do something.

599
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:06,240
You said your team was professional.
How could they just abandon the job?

600
00:43:08,680 --> 00:43:11,560
Madam, my team didn't abandon anything.

601
00:43:11,640 --> 00:43:13,360
They're just tied up
with a bigger project.

602
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:15,440
What do you mean?

603
00:43:15,520 --> 00:43:17,680
My grandpa hired them to work here.

604
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:20,400
How can you say they're busy
with a bigger job?

605
00:43:20,480 --> 00:43:22,320
Miss, you have to understand.

606
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:24,440
Small subcontractors

607
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:27,360
have to keep working
so they can pay their crews.

608
00:43:27,960 --> 00:43:30,560
But there's work here.
Why aren't they doing it?

609
00:43:30,640 --> 00:43:34,040
To be frank, madam,
the wages here are low.

610
00:43:34,760 --> 00:43:36,400
If another place pays more,

611
00:43:36,480 --> 00:43:38,440
they're obviously going to work there.

612
00:43:38,520 --> 00:43:41,000
Think about it.

613
00:43:41,080 --> 00:43:42,600
If it were you, wouldn't you go?

614
00:43:43,600 --> 00:43:46,880
But they agreed to this rate
before accepting the job.

615
00:43:46,960 --> 00:43:49,320
Now somewhere else offers more

616
00:43:49,400 --> 00:43:51,920
and they abandon us?
That's completely irresponsible.

617
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:54,160
I don't care. You personally guaranteed

618
00:43:54,240 --> 00:43:56,160
your team was professional.

619
00:43:56,240 --> 00:43:59,600
My daughter and I put our reputations
on the line for Father to trust you.

620
00:44:00,640 --> 00:44:03,480
Do whatever you have to do. Drag them
back here and get them working.

621
00:44:04,080 --> 00:44:05,640
I've already done everything I can.

622
00:44:05,720 --> 00:44:08,240
I threatened them, begged them.

623
00:44:08,320 --> 00:44:12,000
I practically crawled on my knees
asking them to come back.

624
00:44:12,080 --> 00:44:14,160
So there's no solution?

625
00:44:15,240 --> 00:44:16,720
I think

626
00:44:17,360 --> 00:44:19,160
there is.

627
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:22,480
What do I have to do to get them back?

628
00:44:23,120 --> 00:44:25,560
Right now, there aren't any
economic stimulus measures

629
00:44:25,640 --> 00:44:29,200
or price controls.

630
00:44:29,280 --> 00:44:32,160
Gas, transportation,
everything is expensive.

631
00:44:32,240 --> 00:44:35,280
Most importantly,
the cost of living is high.

632
00:44:35,360 --> 00:44:36,800
Wait.

633
00:44:36,880 --> 00:44:39,960
What does that have to do
with our workers?

634
00:44:40,040 --> 00:44:43,320
When everything costs more,
wages go up too.

635
00:44:44,280 --> 00:44:45,640
You don't understand a thing.

636
00:44:47,280 --> 00:44:49,960
Madam, I think you need
to increase their pay.

637
00:44:51,080 --> 00:44:53,640
Pay more than everyone else.
I'm sure they'll come back.

638
00:44:54,440 --> 00:44:56,280
But what we're paying
is already high enough.

639
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:57,520
Madam,

640
00:44:58,040 --> 00:45:00,720
if Mr. Pichai calls Ramil in
and has him bring everyone back,

641
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:02,400
he'll take control of the whole project.

642
00:45:03,080 --> 00:45:05,120
He'll get all the credit.

643
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:06,920
Think carefully about that.

644
00:45:08,240 --> 00:45:10,640
Whatever they want, pay it.

645
00:45:10,720 --> 00:45:12,360
But they have to come back tomorrow.

646
00:45:15,040 --> 00:45:17,040
Now that's what I call generosity.

647
00:45:17,640 --> 00:45:20,120
A true champion of the workers.

648
00:45:20,200 --> 00:45:23,400
I'll thank you

649
00:45:23,480 --> 00:45:24,760
on their behalf, miss.

650
00:45:24,840 --> 00:45:26,320
And thank you too, madam.

651
00:45:28,200 --> 00:45:29,520
Servant.

652
00:45:34,520 --> 00:45:38,240
Madam, should I call them right now?

653
00:45:40,360 --> 00:45:42,840
Madam agreed to raise your pay.

654
00:45:42,920 --> 00:45:45,040
Get out of there and come back.

655
00:45:45,600 --> 00:45:48,440
Yeah. It's fine.

656
00:45:48,520 --> 00:45:49,440
Yeah, all right.

657
00:45:53,480 --> 00:45:54,480
Done, madam.

658
00:46:02,280 --> 00:46:04,560
You promised to pay them more.

659
00:46:04,640 --> 00:46:06,360
Where do we get that extra money?

660
00:46:06,440 --> 00:46:09,480
Move money from another budget for now.

661
00:46:10,760 --> 00:46:12,960
Did you forget?

662
00:46:13,040 --> 00:46:15,040
Grandpa doesn't let me control
the accounts anymore.

663
00:46:16,640 --> 00:46:19,720
Then use your own money first.

664
00:46:21,600 --> 00:46:23,040
Then I'll be broke.

665
00:46:23,120 --> 00:46:26,440
Mom, you have to invest.

666
00:46:26,520 --> 00:46:29,240
No matter how much money
you have to put in, you have to do it.

667
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:31,840
We need to outperform Ramil and Hathaya.

668
00:46:31,920 --> 00:46:34,960
What we're really betting on
is Grandpa's inheritance.

669
00:46:35,040 --> 00:46:36,560
We can afford to lose this much

670
00:46:36,640 --> 00:46:38,960
if it means getting
everything Grandpa owns.

671
00:46:44,600 --> 00:46:46,360
Sorry, madam.

672
00:46:47,320 --> 00:46:49,600
But something smells fishy.

673
00:46:49,680 --> 00:46:50,760
What?

674
00:46:51,880 --> 00:46:53,920
Can you really trust Pong?

675
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:56,320
What if tomorrow or the next day,

676
00:46:56,400 --> 00:46:58,320
he asks for another raise?

677
00:47:00,040 --> 00:47:01,240
You're right.

678
00:47:02,280 --> 00:47:04,640
You don't look smart,

679
00:47:04,720 --> 00:47:05,840
but you are.

680
00:47:06,840 --> 00:47:07,880
You complimented me.

681
00:47:10,880 --> 00:47:13,160
Keep an eye on him.

682
00:47:13,240 --> 00:47:14,880
If anything happens, report it to me.

683
00:47:14,960 --> 00:47:16,560
It warms my heart that you

684
00:47:16,640 --> 00:47:19,520
finally recognize my talent
for investigating.

685
00:47:20,240 --> 00:47:23,360
Yes. You're number one at sticking
your nose where it doesn't belong.

686
00:47:24,640 --> 00:47:26,400
Thank you.

687
00:47:28,720 --> 00:47:29,840
Was that an insult?

688
00:47:31,280 --> 00:47:35,520
Whatever. I'll prove

689
00:47:35,600 --> 00:47:39,120
that I investigate. I don't pry.

690
00:47:41,960 --> 00:47:43,440
Everything went according to plan.

691
00:47:43,960 --> 00:47:45,320
I told you guys to stop working,

692
00:47:46,800 --> 00:47:48,960
and she immediately raised the wages.

693
00:47:52,480 --> 00:47:54,760
Come early tomorrow. Bring all your stuff.

694
00:47:55,400 --> 00:47:57,640
I'll find another excuse
to get you another raise.

695
00:47:59,080 --> 00:48:00,880
Okay. That's the plan. See you tomorrow.

696
00:48:14,880 --> 00:48:17,480
He was just here. Where did he go?

697
00:48:28,080 --> 00:48:29,280
Looking for someone, Auntie?

698
00:48:29,360 --> 00:48:31,840
No. I'm not looking for anyone.

699
00:48:31,920 --> 00:48:34,440
I was just taking a walk.

700
00:48:34,960 --> 00:48:37,400
I was born

701
00:48:37,480 --> 00:48:39,840
at a construction site, you know.

702
00:48:39,920 --> 00:48:43,360
I love the smell of cement and dirt.

703
00:48:45,240 --> 00:48:48,600
It's so refreshing. Reminds me

704
00:48:49,480 --> 00:48:51,520
of my mom and dad.

705
00:48:52,720 --> 00:48:54,560
You miss your mom and dad that much?

706
00:48:55,680 --> 00:48:57,240
Yeah. A lot.

707
00:49:02,280 --> 00:49:03,440
Then…

708
00:49:05,520 --> 00:49:06,440
how about…

709
00:49:08,640 --> 00:49:12,040
I take you to see them? I'll help you out.

710
00:49:13,320 --> 00:49:15,600
No. That's okay.

711
00:49:15,680 --> 00:49:17,680
I'm not ready to go yet.

712
00:49:18,920 --> 00:49:20,080
You sure?

713
00:49:20,160 --> 00:49:21,360
Yes.

714
00:49:22,120 --> 00:49:24,320
I think I'll

715
00:49:24,840 --> 00:49:27,880
take my walk over there instead.
Something about this area

716
00:49:28,400 --> 00:49:30,040
suddenly doesn't feel very healthy.

717
00:49:31,560 --> 00:49:33,720
It's a construction site, Auntie.

718
00:49:33,800 --> 00:49:35,040
Not a place for a stroll.

719
00:49:35,120 --> 00:49:37,520
Right. Construction site.

720
00:49:39,800 --> 00:49:41,120
Keep prying into my business

721
00:49:42,400 --> 00:49:44,240
and you're going to die badly, you hag.

722
00:49:47,360 --> 00:49:50,360
Madam, Ramil's real wife is here.

723
00:49:50,440 --> 00:49:51,960
She's been going around telling everyone

724
00:49:52,040 --> 00:49:54,160
she's Ramil's wife.

725
00:49:54,240 --> 00:49:56,000
Are you still angry with me

726
00:49:56,080 --> 00:49:59,120
because I like Raiwin,
the same man you like?

727
00:49:59,200 --> 00:50:02,200
Raiwin wasn't interested in you,
so you went back to Ramil.

728
00:50:02,280 --> 00:50:03,240
You really are something.

729
00:50:03,320 --> 00:50:05,280
‎NEXT EPISODE

730
00:50:05,360 --> 00:50:07,680
Mom, I hate her.

731
00:50:08,680 --> 00:50:10,720
-Grandpa!
-Sir!

732
00:52:06,840 --> 00:52:08,840
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
